  "decision_conditions": [
    "The first floor side extension, by reason of bulk, mass, siting, scale and design, would present a two-storey&amp;nbsp;side extension with multiple&amp;nbsp;separate roof forms&amp;nbsp;and unaligned fenestration which would create a disjointed and fragmented appearance. It would also close off the openness of the cornerplot&amp;nbsp;and further balance the uniformity&amp;nbsp;of the terrace row. This would pose harm to the character of the dwelling and on the non-designated heritage&amp;nbsp;asset. The proposal is therefore contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2024) Policies D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD4, DMD5 and Part 6 of SPP6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
